2026-09-27T07:22:14.6864519Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6865016Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6865447Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6866652Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6868236Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6868371Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6868640Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6869046Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6869447Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6869582Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6869881Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6870059Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6870287Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6870832Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6871151Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6871310Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6871735Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6871983Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6872182Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6872833Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6873338Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6874315Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6875202Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6875383Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6876070Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6877116Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6877588Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6878172Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6878865Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6878999Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6879298Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6879475Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6881698Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6884002Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6884353Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6885141Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6886388Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6972675Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6974021Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6974808Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6975271Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6975946Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6976303Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6976522Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6978339Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6980189Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6981185Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6982529Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:14.6982842Z 
